+generated: { by: claude-fable/5.1, at: 2026-09-25T04:51:39.098Z }
+---
+
+# Personal API tokens for the JSON API
+
+## Context
+
+Authors publish from scripts (cron jobs, CI steps) by replaying login cookies
+against the HTML pages, which breaks on every markup change. They need JSON
+endpoints with credentials they create and revoke themselves, and ops wants a
+cap on how hard any one script can hit the site.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Tokens live in `api_tokens`, read through the [ApiToken](../../app/Models/ApiToken.ts)
+  model and written only by the framework's `createApiToken()` through the
+  store in [apiTokenStore.ts](../../app/Auth/apiTokenStore.ts). The row holds a
+  SHA-256 of the secret half; the plain `{id}|{secret}` string is returned once
+  by `POST /profile/tokens` and never persisted.
+- [AuthProvider](../../app/Providers/AuthProvider.ts) registers the store with
+  `auth.useTokens()`, so a request carrying `Authorization: Bearer` resolves to
+  the token guard and `this.auth.user()` is the owner. Cookie-less bearer
+  requests skip CSRF; everything else keeps the session guard.
+- [routes/api.ts](../../routes/api.ts) mounts `/api/posts` (list, create) behind
+  `requireAuthenticated()` (401 JSON, no redirect) and a rate limit of 60
+  requests per minute keyed by token id, so two tokens of one user each get
+  their own window and a limited script reads `Retry-After`.
+- Revocation is scoped to the owner: another user's id answers 404 and leaves
+  the token valid.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The rate limiter uses the in-memory store, which is per process. A
+  multi-process deployment needs a shared `RateLimitStore` (Redis) passed to
+  `createRateLimitMiddleware()` in `routes/api.ts`.
+- Scopes, expiry, and editing or deleting posts over the API are deliberately
+  out of scope; the `abilities` and `expires_at` columns exist because the
+  framework store expects them, and every token is issued with `['*']` and no
+  expiry.
